            <ArticleTitle>Combined anterior-posterior fusion with laterally placed threaded interbody cages and pedicle screws for Scheuermann kyphosis. Case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report their preferred method for correcting Scheuermann disease via a combined anterior-posterior approach; their procedure is associated with a lower morbidity rate than the standard approach. Twenty-month followup examination demonstrated excellent maintenance of correction. The results satisfied the requirements to function without restriction in a vigorous military environment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
